  "question": {
    "text": "The value of $\\int \\cos (\\log x) \\mathrm{d} \\mathrm{x}$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "6A09L",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}[\\sin (\\log x)+\\cos (\\log x)]+C$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "095Eh",
      "text": "$\\frac{x}{2}[\\sin (\\log x)+\\cos (\\log x)]+C$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "F4kTd",
      "text": "$\\frac{x}{2}[\\sin (\\log x)-\\cos (\\log x)]+C$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AHqyU",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}[\\sin (\\log x)-\\cos (\\log x)]+C$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let\r\n\r\n\\(\\mathrm{I}=\\int \\cos (\\log \\mathrm{x}) \\cdot 1 \\mathrm{~d} \\mathrm{x} \\ldots . . \\text { (i) }\\)\r\n\r\nUse integral by parts,\r\n\r\n\\(\\begin{aligned} &I=\\cos (\\log x) \\cdot x-\\int[-\\sin (\\log x)] \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\cdot x d x \\\\ &=x \\cdot \\cos (\\log x)+\\int \\sin (\\log x) \\cdot 1 d x \\\\ &=x \\cdot \\cos (\\log x)+\\left[\\sin (\\log x) \\cdot x-\\int \\cos (\\log x) \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\cdot x d x\\right]+C \\\\ &=x \\cdot(\\log x)+\\left[x \\sin (\\log x)-\\int \\cos (\\log x) d x\\right]+C \\\\ &=x\\{\\sin (\\log x)+\\cos (\\log x)\\}-I+C[f r o m \\text { Eq. (i) }] \\\\ &\\Rightarrow I=\\frac{x}{2}\\{\\sin (\\log x)+\\cos (\\log x)\\}+C \\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
